{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06NQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX \\ar[rr]_f \\ar[rd]_p & &\nY \\ar[dl]^q \\\\\n& B\n}\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$p$", "MATH_0006": "$q$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-syntomic-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8abaef2acafdeb34050a65dff0631fdff917d189b8ce51bb630393cc8b22788c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4b0dfc4186062b6d8dff95a35eca095247c7ccd23d260e9a5b24bd8cbcb0c95c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let\n<MATH_0002>\nbe a commutative diagram of morphisms of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0003>. Assume that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is surjective, flat, and locally of finite presentation,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0005> is syntomic.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nThen both <MATH_0006> and <MATH_0007> are syntomic.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8fdd14914361e8bc1a5b85648f7493bd1aad66397f2ca797566bd8fe8e2eb1fd", "unit_id": "tag:0AHF:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06NQ", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$B$", "MATH_0002": "$Y$", "MATH_0003": "$B$", "MATH_0004": "$Y$", "MATH_0005": "$|X| \\to |Y|$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0008": "$U \\to Y$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-syntomic-local}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-fppf-open}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{descent-lemma-syntomic-permanence}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:87578af789e2474d524ffeea733a380801e777372c9e51b5449ddd2143052682", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7d965da754fb5d7c0286a2e22334ceb49ca6be9530cb17631116119144385230", "source_text": "We deduce this from the analogue for schemes.\nNamely, the problem is <ACCENT_0001>tale local on <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002>\n(Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0001>).\nHence we may assume that <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004> are affine\nschemes. Since <MATH_0005> is open\n(Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0002>),\nwe can choose an affine\nscheme <MATH_0006> and an <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism <MATH_0007> such that the\ncomposition <MATH_0008> is surjective. In this case the result\nfollows from Descent, Lemma\n<REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a975e1300170157803ee966b2047e943493999e38c09b81bfdd29ef67d59e10c", "unit_id": "tag:0AHF:proof"}
